==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|percussio|percussiō|striking|lang=la}}, from {{term|percutio|percutiō|I strike|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|percussions|-}}

# {{context|countable}} the [[collision]] of two [[bodies]] in order to produce a [[sound]]
# {{context|countable}} the sound so produced
# {{context|countable}} the [[detonation]] of a [[percussion cap]] in a [[firearm]]
# {{context|medicine}} the [[tapping]] of the [[body]] as an aid to [[medical]] [[diagnosis]]
# {{context|music}} the section of an [[orchestra]] or band containing [[percussion instrument]]s; such instruments considered as a group
# {{context|engineering}} the repeated striking of an object to break or shape it, as in percussion drilling

